        {
          "id": "a543e9e4-f7e5-4044-8508-9ac6e0a69117",
          "name": "CreateGenerativeExchangeSSE",
          "request": {
            "name": "CreateGenerativeExchangeSSE",
            "description": {
              "content": "CreateGenerativeExchangeSSE Service:\nThis service sends GenerativeExchangeSSEData messages with DELTA state as \"Data-Only\" Server-Sent Events (SSE) when available. The stream terminates with a GenerativeExchangeSSEData message containing the COMPLETE state.\nEach message is sent approximately within a second or less of each other. If clients do not receive a message within their specified timeout, they should assume the connection is lost and attempt to reconnect.\nReference:\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html#server-sent-events\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Server-sent_events/Using_server-sent_events#event_stream_format\nThe following sequence of messages is sent for a single exchange request:\n1. Clients establish a connection to the service by issuing a POST request to the /api/conversation/v1/generative-exchanges/sse endpoint.\n2. The server processes the request and sends a response with a 200 OK status code, Content-Type header set to text/event-stream, and the first \"Data-Only\" message with a state of \"DELTA\". Notes that there is no Metadata or Reference in \"DELTA\" messages.\n\nExample Messages:\nMessage 1: data: {\"state\": 2,\"data\": {\"text\": \"hello\"}}\nMessage 2: data: {\"state\": 2,\"data\": {\"text\": \" \"}}\nMessage 3: data: {\"state\": 2,\"data\": {\"text\": \"world\"}}\nMessage 4: data: {\"state\": 2,\"data\": {\"text\": \"!\"}}\n\nThe final message is sent when the service has completely processed the generative exchange request, and the server terminates the stream.\nThe final message contains a state of COMPLETE, and the GenerativeExchangeSSEData includes the entire text output of the exchange request (including Reference if there is any) as if it was created by the REST API (POST /api/conversation/v1/generative-exchanges).\n\nMessage 5 (final message): data: {\"metadata\": {...},\"state\": 3,\"data\": {\"text\": \"hello world!\",\"reference\": [{\"text_index_start\": 0,\"text_index_stop\": 5,\"exchange_output_index\": 0}]}}",
